  "about": "T1.36 P3 C3's vectors, written by the independent test author before the fix: a struct with a null row holding a union, which run_python's arrow_values must read without aborting (StructArray.flatten() folds the struct's validity into a union child, which has none, and Arrow C++ aborts). The form is contract/t132g-p2c-vectors.json's: a null struct row is null; a non-null one [\"struct\", [[name, cell], ...]]; a union [\"union\", type code, member name, the member's cell], a null union DuckDB writes a null under its first member. A vector with 'sql' runs on DuckDB; one with 'build' is built as Arrow by contract/tests/test_t136_struct_null_union.py (DuckDB writes no dense union): built lists hold their structs at a non-zero offset, so a read that drops a struct's offset gives other cells. Read by the Python runner's test only.",
